# SYNOPSIS

```text
userboot.next=bin/launcher launcher.until=board-test
```

# DESCRIPTION

board-test is the board image's last service: the image a board is booted with to see that it is stable.
The image holds every service, the console among them, but not the test programs, the launcher's own test, or fs(4) and the shell, which wait for a virtio disk a board hasn't.
The launcher runs until board-test ends and exits with its code (launcher(8)); the board image's command line then reboots, so a board whose firmware boots the image once returns to its own system.

It waits up to 30 seconds for devmgr(8) to bind its drivers, then checks that every device devmgr bound has its driver running with its DMA on an IOMMU (not `passthrough` or `none`), and that every IOMMU devmgr names is `ok`.
Then it waits up to 90 seconds from its start for `/net/ether0`'s link to come up and for ip(4) to take an IPv4 address on it, by DHCP or as configured, which needs frames to have gone both ways.
It prints a line for each check, `board-test: ok:` or `board-test: FAILED:` and what it checks, each bound device's line of devmgr's status, each IOMMU, the interface's status, and at the end each driver's own `status`; its last line is `board-test: passed` or `board-test: FAILED, <n> checks`.
It exits 0 if every check passed.

